{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++14 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++14 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\ntypedef long long LL;\ntypedef unsigned long long ULL;\n\nconst LL MOD1 = 998244353LL;\nconst LL MOD2 = 1000000007LL;\n\ninline LL read() {\n    LL x = 0, f = 1;\n    char ch = getchar();\n    while (ch < '0' || ch > '9') { if (ch == '-') f = -1; ch = getchar(); }\n    while (ch >= '0' && ch <= '9') { x = x * 10 + (ch - '0'); ch = getchar(); }\n    return x * f;\n}\n\nLL mod_pow(LL base, LL exp, LL mod) {\n    LL result = 1;\n    base %= mod;\n    while (exp > 0) {\n        if (exp & 1) result = (result * base) % mod;\n        base = (base * base) % mod;\n        exp >>= 1;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nLL N;\nLL counter1 = 0;\nLL first_sum[7];\nvector<LL> first_digits[7];\n\nvoid generate_first(LL depth, LL current) {\n    if (depth > 6) return;\n    first_digits[depth].push_back((counter1 - current + MOD1) % MOD1);\n    first_sum[depth] = (first_sum[depth] + (counter1 - current + MOD1) % MOD1) % MOD1;\n    counter1++;\n    for (LL digit = 0; digit <= 9; ++digit) {\n        generate_first(depth + 1, current * 10 + digit);\n    }\n}\n\nLL counter2 = -1;\nLL answer = 0;\n\nvoid generate_second(LL depth, LL current) {\n    if (current > N) return;\n    \n    if (current * 1000000 + 999999 <= N && current * 10000000 > N) {\n        for (LL d = 0; d <= 6; ++d) {\n            LL needed = ((counter2 + 1 - current * mod_pow(10, d, MOD1) % MOD1) % MOD1 + MOD1) % MOD1;\n            auto it = lower_bound(first_digits[d].begin(), first_digits[d].end(), needed);\n            LL idx = it - first_digits[d].begin();\n            LL contribution = (first_sum[d] + needed * (LL)first_digits[d].size() % MOD1 - MOD1 * (first_digits[d].size() - idx)) % MOD1;\n            answer = (answer + contribution) % MOD2;\n        }\n        counter2 = (counter2 + counter1) % MOD1;\n        return;\n    }\n    \n    counter2 = (counter2 + 1) % MOD1;\n    answer = (answer + ((counter2 - current) % MOD1 + MOD1) % MOD1) % MOD2;\n    \n    for (LL digit = 0; digit <= 9; ++digit) {\n        if (!depth && !digit) continue;\n        generate_second(depth + 1, current * 10 + digit);\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    N = read();\n    generate_first(0, 0);\n    for (LL i = 0; i <= 6; ++i) {\n        sort(first_digits[i].begin(), first_digits[i].end());\n    }\n    generate_second(0, 0);\n    cout << answer << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport bisect\n\nsys.setrecursionlimit(1000000)\n\nMOD1 = 998244353\nMOD2 = 1000000007\n\ndef read():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    return int(data[0])\n\ndef mod_pow(base, exp, mod):\n    result = 1\n    base %= mod\n    while exp > 0:\n        if exp & 1:\n            result = (result * base) % mod\n        base = (base * base) % mod\n        exp >>= 1\n    return result\n\nN = 0\ncounter1 = 0\nfirst_sum = [0] * 7\nfirst_digits = [[] for _ in range(7)]\n\ndef generate_first(depth, current):\n    global counter1\n    if depth > 6